{
 "set": "mount",
 "applies_to": "horse",
 "version": 1,
 "convention": "Targets are angles in degrees relative to the rig's rest pose, which is the square halt (pose stand-square): every value of that pose is zero. Positive means: root.pitch nose up, root.roll left side down, root.yaw turns left, root.lift body raised as a fraction of withers height (0.55 m in game); pelvis.pitch croup tucks under (hindquarters lower), pelvis.roll left hip lower, pelvis.yaw hips to the left; spine.flex back rounds (arches up), spine.side bends left, spine.twist chest turns left; neck_base.pitch neck raised, yaw/roll to the left; poll.pitch nose tucks in (head flexed down), yaw/roll to the left; tail.lift raised, tail.swing to the left; fore shoulder = limb swings forward, elbow/carpus/fetlock = flexion (fetlock + also means the toe drops), abd = limb away from the midline; hind hip = limb swings forward, stifle/hock/fetlock = flexion, abd away from the midline. Sides are the horse's own left and right. Rest absolute flexions for conversion: front fetlock 20, carpus 0, elbow 5; hind fetlock 25, hock 30, stifle 35; neck 40 above horizontal.",
 "joint_source": "Joint keys are anatomical, not the rig's bone names, because the Paladin horse rig (t1-horse-v1) is only specified (GOAL-PROMPT-LAYERED.md line 100) and not built: a mesh-only horse blend exists. Planned rig layout (upstream horse adapter, eternum-knight-pr-r2 apps/game/src/three/characters/horse/horse-rig-adapter.ts): root, pelvis, spine, chest, withers, neck x2, head, four legs, tail x3, tack bones. Map: root=root, pelvis=pelvis, spine=spine+chest, neck_base=first neck bone, poll=head; front leg shoulder/elbow/carpus/fetlock = frontShoulder/frontUpper/frontLower/(hoof); hind hip/stifle/hock/fetlock = hindShoulder/hindUpper/hindMiddle/hindLower. Where the final rig has fewer bones, fold the pair (elbow into shoulder, fetlock into the lowest bone) at import.",
